## DESCRIPTION
## WeBWorK Demo
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('lines')
## Tagged by jjh2b

## DBsubject('WeBWorK')
## DBchapter('Linears and Linear Function')
## DBsection('Problem')
## Date('September 5, 2008')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric")->variables->add(y => 'Real', z => 'Real');
Context()->noreduce('(-x)-y', '(-x)+y');

($a1, $b1, $c1) = (random(1, 6), random(1, 6), random(1, 6));
($a2, $b2, $c2) = (random(1, 6), random(1, 6), random(1, 6));
($a,  $b,  $c)  = (random(1, 6), random(1, 6), random(1, 6));

$d1 = 5 * random(2, 6);
$d2 = 3 * $d1;

$f1  = Formula("$a1 x + $b1 y + $c1 z")->reduce;
$f2  = Formula("$a2 x + $b2 y + $c2 z")->reduce;
$obj = Formula("$a x + $b y + $c z")->reduce;

Context('Matrix');
$m = Matrix([
    [ $a1,  $b1,  $c1,  1, 0,, 0, 0, $d1 ],
    [ -$a2, -$b2, -$c2, 0, 1, 0, 0, -$d2 ],
    [ 1,    -1,   0,    0, 0,  1, 0, 0 ],
    [ $a,   $b,   $c,   0, 0,  0, 1, 0 ]
]);

BEGIN_PGML
The following linear programming problem is a *nonstandard* problem:

Minimize [`f(x, y, z) = [$obj] `] subject to
[```
\begin{cases}
[$f1] \leq [$d1] \\
[$f2] \geq [$d2] \\
x \leq y, \\
x \geq 0, \; y \geq 0, \; z \geq 0.
\end{cases}
```]

Write the simplex tableau down for this problem:

[_]*{$m}

END_PGML

$negf2  = Compute("-$a2 x-$b2 y - $c2 z")->reduce;
$negobj = Compute("-$a x -$b y -$c z")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
We need to write this in standard form. The objective to be maximized is
[``` p = [$negobj]```]

First, start by writing the three inequalities such that they are written in the form [`\leq b`], for some constant [`b`].
[```
\begin{aligned}
[$f1] &\leq [$d1] \\
[$negf2] &\leq [@-$d2@] \\
x -y &\leq 0 \\
\end{aligned}
```]

Next, write these down as equations using slack variables.  We'll use [`s_1, s_2`] and [`s3`].
[```
\begin{aligned}
[$f1] + s_1 &= [$d1] \\
[$negf2] + s_2 &= [@-$d2@] \\
x -y + s_3 & = 0 \\
\end{aligned}
```]
and then rewrite the objective as
[``` [$obj]+p = 0```]

These are then put into a matrix/tableau as
[``` [$m] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
